# One line-ending rule for the whole tree.
#
# The repo had accumulated a mix - 58 of 201 tracked files were CRLF, including
# vald.service and half the templates - with no pattern to it. The cost was not
# cosmetic: any tool that rewrites a file whole (an editor, a script, a
# refactor) silently converted it to LF, so a three-line change arrived as a
# diff of the entire file and buried the real edit. That happened three times
# during the pre-launch review.
#
# text=auto lets git detect binary content and leave it alone; eol=lf sets the
# working-tree ending on every platform, which is what both macOS and the Linux
# server want.
* text=auto eol=lf

# The binary formats actually present, marked explicitly rather than relying on
# the heuristic - a corrupted PNG is a silent, ugly failure.
*.png binary
*.ico binary
